@page "/data-deletion"

<PageTitle>Account and Data Deletion | It's a Budget</PageTitle>
<HeadContent>
    <meta name="description" content="How to request deletion of an It's a Budget account, connected-bank access, and associated data." />
</HeadContent>

<article class="public-page">
    <p class="public-page-kicker">YOUR DATA</p>
    <h1>Account and Data Deletion</h1>
    <p class="lead">
        You may request removal of your It's a Budget account and associated
        personal information, subject to legal, security, and backup-retention
        requirements.
    </p>

    <h2>Disconnect a bank first</h2>
    <p>
        Signed-in users can open <strong>Accounts → Bank Connections</strong> and
        remove a Plaid connection. This revokes the application's active
        connection and stops future synchronization for that item. Information
        already used in your checkbook remains until it is separately deleted.
    </p>

    <h2>Request account deletion</h2>
    <ol>
        <li>Use the <a href="/contact">contact instructions</a>.</li>
        <li>Identify the username for the account you want removed.</li>
        <li>Do not send passwords, bank credentials, Plaid tokens, or full account numbers.</li>
        <li>Complete a reasonable identity-verification step if requested.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>What the request covers</h2>
    <p>
        A verified request may cover the user profile, external-login link,
        notification settings, personal financial records, attachments, Plaid
        connections, and memberships that can be removed without improperly
        deleting another member's shared records.
    </p>

    <h2>Shared budgets and retained records</h2>
    <p>
        Shared-budget information may belong to more than one member. The
        operator may remove your membership or de-identify your contribution
        rather than delete records another authorized member still needs.
        Limited information may also be retained for security, fraud
        prevention, dispute resolution, legal compliance, and backup rotation.
    </p>

    <h2>Timing</h2>
    <p>
        Requests will be acknowledged and processed within a reasonable period.
        Deletion from active systems may occur before limited-retention backup
        copies expire.
    </p>
</article>
